Practical 2: DataFrame Creation and Statistical Summary
Aim: Create a DataFrame with at least five observations, retrieve a particular column, summarize the DataFrame, and calculate the mean and standard deviation.

Dataset: Iris dataset from Scikit-learn.
Complete Python program


import pandas as pd
from sklearn.datasets import load_iris

# Load the real Iris dataset
iris = load_iris(as_frame=True)

# Select the first 10 observations
df = iris.frame.head(10).copy()

# Add species names
df["Species"] = df["target"].map(
    dict(enumerate(iris.target_names))
)

# Remove the numeric target column
df.drop(columns=["target"], inplace=True)

# Display the complete DataFrame
print("DataFrame:")
print(df.to_string(index=False))

# Retrieve a particular column
print("\nSepal Length Column:")
print(df["sepal length (cm)"].to_string(index=False))

# Display summary statistics
print("\nSummary Statistics:")
print(df.describe())

# Calculate the mean of numeric columns
print("\nMean:")
print(df.mean(numeric_only=True))

# Calculate the standard deviation
print("\nStandard Deviation:")
print(df.std(numeric_only=True))



The ellipses above indicate omitted rows and columns for readability; running the program prints the complete output.

Result: A DataFrame was created from real Iris observations, and column retrieval, summary statistics, mean and standard deviation were demonstrated successfully.
